JSON-RPC protocol, not MCP, and the removal commit names no successor.
`codex mcp` is only for managing external servers Codex connects to.

## Hints for Future Agents
- The repo had a pre-existing unmerged index entry for claude_settings.json
  (UU) with no MERGE_HEAD and no conflict markers in the file, plus unrelated
  .tmux.conf edits. `git commit -- <paths>` still works in that state: it
  prints "claude_settings.json: needs merge" but commits the named paths. Do
  not resolve or commit those files; they are the user's in-flight work.
- install.sh sets .mcpServers wholesale with jq, so any server removed from
  ~/.claude.json by hand comes back on the next install.sh run unless it is
  also removed there.
- ~/.claude.json is rewritten by running Claude Code sessions. Hand edits can
  be clobbered; restart is required for MCP changes to take effect anyway.

## Codebase Discoveries
- rules/ is symlinked to ~/.claude/rules, while commands, skills, and agents
  come from the abatilo-core plugin. install.sh concatenates a hand-listed
  subset of rules/*.md into ~/.codex/AGENTS.md, so adding a rule file does not
  reach Codex unless the loop is edited too.
- The Codex CLI install stays: AGENTS.md generation and the repo-explore and
  speed-of-light skills copied into ~/.codex/skills.

